LOGBOOK.md:10:- DECISION: The macOS-first M0 Bridge gate passes under ADR-024 with MTU 1500, requested/effective 32768-byte socket buffers, 64-packet/5-ms pump budgets, HEV task-stack/TCP/UDP-copy values 24576/4096/2, and an initial measured 500-session ceiling. MTU 4096 remains injectable behind end-to-end proof; MTU 8500 is a named failed default candidate because constrained-buffer rows produced 768 `EMSGSIZE` refusals.
LOGBOOK.md:11:- EVIDENCE: Public-API bridge, IPv4/IPv6 framing, deterministic faults, hostile-frame fuzzing, bounded pressure, lifecycle, packaging, notices, and physical Mac MTU/memory rows trace to accepted task-scoped resources in `docs/TASK-260715-2jatnd_m0-bridge-hev-decision-adr.md`. The worst measured incremental HEV/bridge cost was 9,715,712 bytes at 500 sessions; whole-extension SSH/DNS/relay/cache/reconnect memory remains unmeasured.
LOGBOOK.md:18:- ROOT CAUSE: The rev3 gate coupled two distinct claims. Harness-owned channels, reads, queues, boundary/native lifecycle counters, and descriptor-close stages were released deterministically, but the gate still required Darwin to return allocator pages during the same 500-cycle observation. One reviewer run therefore failed on a bounded `+180224 B` non-decreasing footprint rise while the next two passed.
LOGBOOK.md:19:- FIX: The schema-2 lifecycle evidence now records an `ownedResourcesReleased` verdict and every underlying ownership field for each cycle. The production gate requires 500 cycles, zero failed owned-resource-release cycles, and the unchanged post-warmup maximum resident-footprint drawup ceiling of `256 KiB`. Monotonic and late rises remain classified with exact transition/cycle evidence, but OS page-return timing is no longer used as a proxy for product-owned release. The matrix atomically emits its exact-tree-bound raw report before returning a failing verdict.
LOGBOOK.md:21:- EXPLORATORY MEASUREMENT: A fresh exact-tree 500-cycle loopback probe reproduced the allocator ambiguity with `+147480 B` net change and `180248 B` maximum drawup while all `500/500` cycles restored every owned resource. Descriptors returned from 9 to 3, threads from 9 to 7, and the deterministic release gate passed. This supports signal separation without widening the 500-cycle or 256 KiB bounds.
LOGBOOK.md:24:- ROOT CAUSE/FIX: `measureRealHEVLifecycle` retained every sample in an initially empty Swift `Array` after taking its baseline. The observer now reserves the exact bounded cycle count before the baseline snapshot. A production-call-site regression asserts capacity for 1000 samples, and the diagnostic entry accepts only 100/500/1000 cycles; malformed or wider values fail closed.
LOGBOOK.md:25:- MEASUREMENT: Corrected exact-tree loopback probes ran 100/500/1000 real HEV cycles. Post-warmup net change was `+81,944 B` / `-212,992 B` / `-32,768 B`; maximum drawup was `98,328 B` / `65,536 B` / `65,536 B`; increase/equal/decrease transitions were `3/85/1`, `4/479/6`, and `7/977/5`. The prior late approximately 16 KiB jumps above cycle 1000 disappeared; the last 1000-cycle increase was cycle 481. Every sample restored live sessions, reads, and queues to zero; descriptors ended at 3 and threads at 8.
LOGBOOK.md:26:- RULE: A fresh production-entry repeat proved 100 cycles insufficient: it stopped fail-closed on one `+65,536 B` increase and no release. The simplest repeatable gate therefore uses the next predeclared row, 500 cycles, after fixed 10-sample warmup. It permits a full plateau or a measured release only while maximum drawup stays within 256 KiB (1% of the upper 25 MiB target); late unreleased rise and a released-but-over-ceiling linear sawtooth fail closed. The earlier 2000-cycle/trailing-1000 rule measured observer allocation and is retired rather than widened further.
LOGBOOK.md:29:- INVESTIGATION: A bounded process-local 2000-cycle SwiftPM/loopback run captured every physical-footprint jump and 100-cycle segment. The sampler observed both rises and releases, including `-1,196,032 B` and `-1,130,496 B` segments; post-warmup net change was `-2,310,120 B`. Across the last 500 samples, net change was `-65,536 B` and range was `98,304 B`. Descriptors stayed `3`, threads stayed within `6...8`, and every post-cleanup HEV session, read, and queue count was zero. Boundary start/stop and HEV start/main-return counters were exactly one per cycle. Earlier 500- and 1000-cycle repeats still had late rises, proving neither duration alone established convergence.
LOGBOOK.md:36:- STOP: Three independent 100-cycle physical-Mac probes all failed the corrected gate: `+81,920 B` with `4/85/0`, `+81,920 B` with `5/84/0`, and `+98,328 B` with `4/85/0` increase/equal/decrease transitions. Per rev3 instructions, the 100/250/500 matrix and full suite were not run against a known failing lifecycle prerequisite, and the rule was not weakened. No VPN, NetworkExtension, route, DNS, interface, packet-filter, SSH, or global-memory-pressure operation ran.
LOGBOOK.md:39:- MEASUREMENT: A physical Mac15,9 (arm64, macOS 26.5) SwiftPM run admitted 100, 250, and the explicitly narrowed 500-session ceiling with zero bridge drops. Physical footprint was 12,354,160 B, 15,270,512 B, and 20,038,256 B; peak was 20,054,640 B. The incremental 500-session HEV/bridge cost was 11,976,704 B, leaving 19,480,576 B inside the provisional 30 MiB envelope. This is not a whole-extension Apple guarantee and does not allocate SSH, DNS, relay, caches, or reconnect overlap.
LOGBOOK.md:47:- MEASUREMENT: The bounded loopback-only SPM harness ran 36 rows on a physical Apple M3 Max Mac (arm64, macOS 26.5): MTU 1500/4096/8500 × IPv4/native IPv6/dual stack × nominal/constrained-buffer/25ms receiver-stall/mixed bidirectional traffic. Nominal and mixed rows delivered 100%; pressure rows produced only named bounded effects and recovered with zero production-owned descriptor delta. Swift-task delta is explicitly unavailable because the synchronous runner owns no tasks; process threads are not treated as a proxy.
LOGBOOK.md:48:- FINDING: Requested/effective buffers matched at 4096, 32768, and 262144 bytes. MTU 8500 with a 4096-byte send buffer produced 768 errno-40 `Message too long` refusals across the three family rows plus receive-queue drops; its maximum successful constrained datagram was 768 bytes. This is distinct from receiver overflow and makes 8500 unsuitable as a default solely because upstream uses it.
LOGBOOK.md:49:- RECOMMENDATION: Keep 1500 as the portable baseline; expose 1500...4096 only as an injectable candidate range when an end-to-end path is proven. Use measured requested buffers 32768...262144 bytes; 4096 remains fault injection. Loopback does not prove external fragmentation/path safety.
LOGBOOK.md:52:- REVISION 3: A reviewer reproduced a post-parse parent swap that redirected the Foundation pathname write outside `.temp`. The production writer now uses no-follow `openat` traversal and an fd-bound atomic rename; production-entry tests reject both `.temp -> /tmp` cross-root escape and post-parse replacement. The 64-packet lower bound now applies a measured 4096-byte receiver-stall fault ceiling to 32-packet dual-stack halves. The rerun passed 477 tests; affected coverage is 85.84% regions, 89.11% functions, and 95.86% lines.
LOGBOOK.md:174:- ROOT CAUSE: A fresh post-review aggregate gate reproduced one final in-scope test race at the historical run-13 position. `automaticKeepaliveSurvivesLongRekey` used at most 500 scheduler yields before reading each `keepalivesSent` counter. Under aggregate load, the automatic task had not emitted `.keepaliveSent` before either assertion, even though the fatal keepalive self-join was fixed and the suite exited normally. Fixed yield counts are not a synchronization boundary.
LOGBOOK.md:231:- DECISION: The 4096-byte bound is checked over the actual binary-property-list representation of the exact three-key `providerConfiguration`, so owner and manager-contract metadata count toward the NetworkExtension envelope. The macOS adapter reads only `NETunnelProviderProtocol.providerConfiguration`; it has no App Group, Keychain, route, network, packet, or profile-write path.
LOGBOOK.md:837:- VERIFICATION: Eighteen admission tests cover below/at/above every independent ceiling, 128/256-way reserve races, 500 release/open and 500 late-callback races, 250 explicit-release/deinit ownership races, ID exhaustion, queued-byte overflow, session-health races, 8,000 sustained pressure rejects alongside 2,000 admitted-flow progress steps, every terminal reason across 320 churn lifecycles, and exact local/exported baseline recovery. The bounded-queue convergence probe passes 20/20 runs; focused normal and TSan admission/diagnostics suites pass; `make validate-core` passes boundary/native gates, 306 tests in 27 suites, and the post-test build; strict recursive Swift format, privacy/boundary, diff, and board validation pass.
LOGBOOK.md:1024:- VERIFICATION: Reviewer independently re-checked spec quotes (relay-protocol.md:110-113, security-privacy.md:59-66), HEV pinned-source bounds (`UDP_BUF_SIZE 1500` at hev-socks5-udp.c:26; stream-fatal `datlen > len − addrlen` at :203-206; `msgv[i].len = UDP_BUF_SIZE` in session-udp fwd_b → 1472 ≤ 1481 worst-case IPv6, reply write 1491 ≤ 1500 by construction), frame arithmetic (max legal body 1733 < floor 2048), reserved bit/type-range vacancy in the frozen binding, all 13 downstream ID-scoped notes, ADR-021 number vacancy, and diagram artifacts. No product code modified; `task-board validate` clean. Evidence: `.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-18owh7/TASK-260715-18owh7_review.md`.
